irement_affected"},"detail":"Typing (setFilter, Menu.qml:796) and opening another menu (setActiveMenu, Menu.qml:804, also reached from goBack) set pendingInitialMenu to empty, so a route summoned during startup never pulls the user out of what they chose, even if they went back to root. The rest of both functions, and the filter, navigation stack and back fallback these requirements state, are unchanged; their Implements lines now also name DK0D.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":796},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":804},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DQ9P","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"setFilter and setActiveMenu each gain one line that drops a waiting route (SW-REQ-260922-DQ9P, SW-REQ-260922-DE93)","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93 is in review.changes (code_changed, matchLevel file).","status":"confirmed"}},{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"SW-REQ-260922-50RE"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"The edited onLoadFailed handler (Menu.qml:1079) carries `Implements: SW-REQ-260922-50RE, SW-REQ-261002-DK0D`, so 50RE (open/close/refresh/ping dispatch) is matched at function level. The handler still empties userMenuItems and rebuilds as before; the added `root.userMenuFailed = true` only feeds menuFilesAnswered. refresh() still reloads both files and open() dispatch is unchanged.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":1079},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-50RE","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"SW-REQ-260922-50RE is a function-level match through the user FileView's onLoadFailed","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-50RE","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"SW-REQ-26